================================================================================

SUMMARY
-------
Native SwiftUI parity of the web `InboxPage` — the top-level Notifications inbox route.
The web page is a thin shell: a `PageContainer` (title + subtitle + copyLink + a "View
archived" action) hosting `<InboxBody archived={false} vehicles={vehicles} rules={rules} />`.
The native page reproduces that exactly: the chrome + the shared `InboxBody` surface.

ARCHITECTURE DECISION (reuse, not duplicate) — DRY / shared-component mandate
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared `InboxBody` SwiftUI surface ALREADY ships natively at
`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/InboxBody*.swift` (committed `570cb3060`
"feat(apps/apple/feature-views): add InboxBody surface (P4)", feature-view 0183) — the
faithful native port of `features/notifications/components/InboxBody.tsx` with its own
`@Observable InboxBodyModel`, filter bar, bulk toolbar, grouped/flat list, day grouping,
freshness chrome, and the four list phases (loading / error / empty / content). It was not
yet hosted by any route (no non-DEBUG `InboxBodyModel(...)` construction existed). This P7
page is its FIRST host — exactly the web composition (`InboxPage` renders `<InboxBody/>`).

  → `NotificationsInboxPage` renders the web `PageContainer` chrome and embeds
    `InboxBody(model:)`. It does NOT re-implement the inbox body (that would duplicate the
    P3 component, violate DRY, and — as the first build proved — collide on the public type
    names `NotificationLogItem` / `NotificationSeverity` / `InboxDayHeader` / `InboxErrorView`
    that `InboxBody`/`OperationsSection`/`NotificationFilterBar` already export).

PATH / NAME RECONCILIATION (same as the sibling AuditLog log)
-------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt path `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Notifications/**` is not a real project.yml
source group. The repo's compiled page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**`
(listed as a `Sources` path, createIntermediateGroups). The page ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Notifications/**`, the faithful equivalent. Type name
`NotificationsInboxPage` (module-scoped; collision-swept — 0 clashes for the final public
names `NotificationsInboxPage` / `NotificationsInboxRouteRegistration` / `NotificationsInboxSample`).

"VIEW ARCHIVED" RECONCILIATION
------------------------------
Web "View archived" is a `<Link to="/notifications/archived">` — a separate web route that
reuses the SAME `InboxBody` with `archived=true`. `/notifications/archived` is NOT a parity
unit and has no Apple route, and `InboxBodyModel` fixes `archived` at init. The faithful
native adaptation: the action rebuilds the body in archived mode IN PLACE (the page swaps the
model + forces a fresh `InboxBody` via `.id(archived)`) — the exact body the web `ArchivedPage`
reuses. The required string `notifications.inbox.viewArchived` renders in the default
(inbox) state; the toggled state shows `notifications.inbox.viewInbox`.

